                    ],
                    [
                      "D",
                      "Ratchet, if present",
                      "Maintains closure at a selected position"
                    ],
                    [
                      "E",
                      "Long jaws",
                      "Apply pressure along the bowel segment"
                    ],
                    [
                      "F",
                      "Jaw surfaces",
                      "Distribute pressure to help occlude the bowel with minimal trauma"
                    ],
                    [
                      "G",
                      "Tips",
                      "Form the terminal ends of the jaws"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The exact jaw profile, length, and locking mechanism depend on the model. Some clamps have straight jaws, while others have curved jaws."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "Properties and construction",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_4",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A non-crushing bowel clamp typically has:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Material: Surgical-grade stainless steel."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Jaws: Long and relatively slender, designed for intestinal occlusion."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Jaw surfaces: May have longitudinal grooves or other patterns intended to distribute pressure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Joint: Allows controlled opening and closure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Locking mechanism: Often includes a ratchet, depending on the model."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Shape: Straight or curved, depending on the intended operative site."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Reusability: Many models are reusable and require appropriate cleaning and sterilization."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The primary design objective is to provide effective temporary occlusion while preserving the integrity and viability of the bowel wall."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "Classification and types",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_5",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/non_crushing_bowel_clamp_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "1. Doyen intestinal clamp"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A commonly encountered atraumatic bowel clamp with long jaws designed to distribute pressure along the bowel."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/non_crushing_bowel_clamp_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "2. Curved atraumatic intestinal clamp"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Curved jaws may facilitate placement in selected operative fields, depending on the bowel anatomy and surgical approach."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/non_crushing_bowel_clamp_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "3. Payr intestinal clamp"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A named intestinal clamp design encountered in surgical instrument classifications. Its precise function and degree of tissue compression should be confirmed from the particular model rather than inferred from the name alone."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "OSCE caution: Do not automatically classify every named intestinal clamp as non-crushing. The intended function depends on the instrument's design and manufacturer specifications."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "Principle of operation",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_6",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The instrument works by controlled compression of the bowel lumen."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The surgeon selects the appropriate bowel segment."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The jaws are placed across the segment to be temporarily occluded."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The clamp is closed using controlled pressure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The bowel lumen is compressed sufficiently to limit passage of intestinal contents."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The clamp is released when occlusion is no longer required."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The jaw design aims to distribute pressure and reduce focal tissue damage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Key principle: Effective occlusion should be achieved with the least pressure necessary, for the shortest clinically appropriate duration."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "Uses and indications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_7",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A non-crushing bowel clamp may be used to:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Temporarily occlude the intestinal lumen."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Limit spillage of bowel contents during selected operations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Isolate bowel segments during resection."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Facilitate preparation of bowel ends for anastomosis."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assist in selected intestinal reconstructive procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Temporarily control intestinal contents during appropriate gastrointestinal operations."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_8",
              "group_title": "Surgeries in which it is used",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Procedure",
                    "Purpose"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Small bowel resection",
                      "Occlude selected bowel segments"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Colectomy",
                      "Temporarily control the bowel lumen during transection"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Intestinal anastomosis",
                      "Reduce passage of contents while bowel ends are prepared"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Emergency laparotomy",
                      "Isolate selected bowel segments when required"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Bowel reconstruction",
                      "Assist temporary occlusion during reconstruction"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The precise application depends on the procedure and the condition of the intestine."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_9",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Reduced crushing injury: Designed to minimize compression damage compared with crushing clamps."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Temporary occlusion: Helps control passage of bowel contents."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Distributed pressure: Long jaws may reduce focal compression."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Improved operative control: Helps isolate selected bowel segments."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Versatility: Available in different sizes and configurations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Reusability: Many models can be reprocessed for repeated use."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "Disadvantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_10",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Excessive pressure can still damage the bowel wall."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Prolonged clamping can compromise perfusion."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inadequate closure may permit intestinal leakage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Incorrect placement may cause the clamp to slip."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Long jaws can be difficult to position in confined spaces."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Fragile or severely inflamed bowel may not tolerate even atraumatic clamping well."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "Complications and risks",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_11",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Explanation"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Bowel wall injury",
                      "Excessive pressure can damage intestinal tissue"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Ischaemia",
                      "Compression may compromise local blood flow"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Serosal injury",
                      "The outer bowel surface may be damaged"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Perforation",
                      "Severe tissue injury may cause a defect in the bowel wall"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Spillage",
                      "Inadequate occlusion may allow intestinal contents to escape"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Clamp slippage",
                      "Incorrect placement may lead to loss of occlusion"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Tissue oedema",
                      "Local compression may contribute to swelling"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Anastomotic complications",
                      "Injury or compromised perfusion may adversely affect healing"
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_12",
              "group_title": "Prevention",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Select an appropriate atraumatic clamp."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check the condition of the bowel before placement."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Apply only the pressure required for occlusion."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Avoid unnecessary prolonged clamping."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ensure the clamp is correctly positioned and stable."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inspect the bowel wall and perfusion after release."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Replace damaged or malfunctioning instruments."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "Non-crushing versus crushing bowel clamp",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_13",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "This is one of the most important viva distinctions."
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Feature",
                    "Non-crushing bowel clamp",
                    "Crushing bowel clamp"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Primary purpose",
                      "Temporary occlusion while preserving tissue",
                      "Firm compression of a bowel segment"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Pressure",
                      "Designed to minimize tissue trauma",
                      "Intentionally applies stronger compression"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Effect on bowel",
                      "Aims to preserve bowel-wall integrity",
                      "May cause substantial tissue damage"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Typical application",
                      "Occlusion during bowel resection and anastomosis",
                      "Selected procedures where crushing the clamped segment is intended"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Tissue preservation",
                      "Important consideration",
                      "The compressed portion may not be suitable for retention"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Exam tip: The terms atraumatic and non-crushing describe the intended effect, not a guarantee that tissue injury cannot occur."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "Precautions and contraindications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_14",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Avoid unnecessary clamping time."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use particular caution with friable, oedematous, inflamed, or ischaemic bowel."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Do not overtighten the clamp."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Confirm that the jaws are appropriately aligned."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Do not use a crushing clamp when the intended technique requires preservation of the clamped bowel."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Follow the manufacturer's instructions and the surgeon's operative plan."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_13",
          "subsection_title": "Care, cleaning and sterilization",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_15",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Remove gross contamination promptly after use."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Open the jaws and ratchet, if present."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Clean the jaw surfaces, grooves, joint, shanks, and handles."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Rinse and dry thoroughly according to the manufacturer's instructions."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inspect for corrosion, deformation, and jaw misalignment."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check that the clamp opens and closes smoothly."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Confirm that the locking mechanism functions properly."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Sterilize using a validated method compatible with the instrument."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_subsection_14",
          "subsection_title": "High-yield OSCE viva questions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "non_crushing_bowel_clamp_group_16",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is a non-crushing bowel clamp?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An intestinal clamp designed to temporarily occlude the bowel lumen while minimizing compression injury to the bowel wall."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. What is its main principle?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Controlled compression of the bowel lumen using jaws designed to distribute pressure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. Give an example of a non-crushing bowel clamp."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The Doyen intestinal clamp is a commonly encountered example."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. What is the difference between a Doyen clamp and the general term non-crushing bowel clamp?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Doyen is a specific named instrument, whereas non-crushing bowel clamp describes a broader functional category of atraumatic intestinal occlusion clamps."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. Mention three indications."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Temporary occlusion during bowel resection, colectomy, and intestinal anastomosis."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. Mention four complications."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Bowel wall injury, ischaemia, serosal damage, and intestinal spillage from inadequate occlusion."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. Why should prolonged clamping be avoided?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Sustained pressure can compromise perfusion and cause bowel-wall injury."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. What should be assessed after releasing the clamp?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The bowel wall should be inspected for injury, and tissue perfusion should be assessed as appropriate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q9. Is a non-crushing clamp completely harmless to bowel tissue?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "No. Excessive pressure, prolonged application, or poor positioning can still cause injury."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q10. What should be inspected before use?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Jaw alignment, jaw surfaces, joint movement, locking mechanism, and any signs of damage or corrosion."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
